---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Perplexity × Samsung · Case study • TheFocus.AI"
  description="Perplexity, in 50 million living rooms — voice-first answers on Samsung Smart TVs, 12 weeks from kickoff to QA approval."
  eyebrow="PERPLEXITY × SAMSUNG · LIVING ROOM"
  heading="Perplexity, in 50 million living rooms."
  heroImage="/assets/cs-perplexity-livingroom.png"
  heroAlt="A glowing TV in a dark living room, seen from behind a sofa"
  meta={[
    { label: "CLIENT", value: "Perplexity AI" },
    { label: "SECTOR", value: "Consumer Electronics · AI" },
    { label: "SERVICES", value: "Strategy + Development" },
    { label: "TIMELINE", value: "12 weeks to Samsung QA" },
  ]}
  moreWork={[
    { href: "/work/ae-networks/", eyebrow: "A+E NETWORKS", title: "Watching 212 data feeds so nobody has to." },
    { href: "/work/steering-house/", eyebrow: "STEERING HOUSE", title: "Construction books that reconcile themselves." },
  ]}
>
  <!-- Editorial body -->
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <p class="text-2xl sm:text-[28px] leading-[1.45] text-[#E5E5E5] tracking-tight">
      Perplexity wanted to bring their answer engine into the living room, on Samsung's 50-million-household Smart TV
      platform. A TV has no keyboard, no touchscreen, and a remote with about five useful buttons.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14">
      <div class="mono text-xs text-[#556B2F] tracking-[1.5px] mb-4">THE CHALLENGE</div>
      <p class="text-[#B0B0B0] text-[17px] leading-relaxed">
        Typing a question with an on-screen keyboard and a d-pad takes forever — nobody does it twice. Every part of
        the experience had to work from ten feet away, navigated with up/down/left/right and a back button, on hardware
        with a fraction of a phone's processing power. And before any of it could ship, it had to pass Samsung's
        certification process: <span class="text-white"
          >over 100 test cases, covering everything from memory limits to privilege declarations.</span
        >
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="my-14 border-l-2 border-[#556B2F] pl-6">
      <blockquote class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.25] text-white">
        "We didn't adapt a phone app for the TV. We built for the ten-foot experience from day one."
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption class="mono text-[11px] tracking-[1.5px] text-[#666] mt-4">THE FOCUS</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div>
      <div class="mono text-xs text-[#556B2F] tracking-[1.5px] mb-4">WHAT WE BUILT</div>
      <p class="text-[#B0B0B0] text-[17px] leading-relaxed">
        We built a complete spatial focus-navigation system from scratch, before writing a single feature — every
        element on screen declares its neighbors up, down, left, and right, so the remote always moves where you'd
        expect. Voice comes in through the Samsung SmartThings app or a Bluetooth mic, feeds OpenAI's Realtime API for
        speech-to-text, and falls back to the keyboard cleanly if a microphone isn't available.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[#B0B0B0] text-[17px] leading-relaxed">
        Answers stream in word by word rather than waiting for a full response — important on a screen ten feet away,
        where waiting reads as broken. The whole thing shipped in English, German, and Korean at launch, with the
        interface detecting the TV's system language automatically.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Inline full-width image -->
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8">
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/assets/apps/app-samsung.png"
        alt="A smart TV glowing in a dark living room"
        class="w-full h-[40vh] min-h-[280px] object-cover border border-white/10"
      />
      <figcaption class="mono text-[11px] tracking-[1.5px] text-[#666] mt-3">
        EVERY SCREEN FLOW WAS TESTED WITH ONLY ARROW KEYS AND ENTER — BEFORE A MOUSE EVER TOUCHED IT.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <!-- Technical summary -->
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="mono text-xs text-[#556B2F] tracking-[1.5px] mb-6">HOW IT'S BUILT</div>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-px bg-white/10 border border-white/10">
      <div class="bg-[#0A0A0A] p-6">
        <div class="mono text-[10px] tracking-[1.5px] text-[#666] mb-3">FRONTEND</div>
        <div class="text-[#E5E5E5] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          SvelteKit, TypeScript, Tailwind — a custom focus-navigation system built for remote control.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-[#0A0A0A] p-6">
        <div class="mono text-[10px] tracking-[1.5px] text-[#666] mb-3">VOICE</div>
        <div class="text-[#E5E5E5] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          OpenAI Realtime API for speech-to-text, with ephemeral session tokens and automatic keyboard fallback.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-[#0A0A0A] p-6">
        <div class="mono text-[10px] tracking-[1.5px] text-[#666] mb-3">AI INTEGRATION</div>
        <div class="text-[#E5E5E5] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Perplexity's API, streamed as Server-Sent Events with citation deduplication and markdown rendering.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-[#0A0A0A] p-6">
        <div class="mono text-[10px] tracking-[1.5px] text-[#666] mb-3">PLATFORM</div>
        <div class="text-[#E5E5E5] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Tizen SDK, static build pipeline, multi-channel release process (release / develop / test).
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Outcome band -->
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 border-t border-white/10">
      <div class="py-8 sm:pr-8 border-b sm:border-b-0 sm:border-r border-white/10">
        <div class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">50M+ TVs</div>
        <div class="text-[#999] text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">Deployed across Samsung's global Smart TV install base.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="py-8 sm:px-8 border-b sm:border-b-0 sm:border-r border-white/10">
        <div class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Sub-2-second</div>
        <div class="text-[#999] text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">From button press to voice recognition starting to listen.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="py-8 sm:pl-8">
        <div class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">First submission</div>
        <div class="text-[#999] text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">Passed Samsung's QA certification on the first major submission.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>
